GPUI Kit integrations and editor overlays
Sailry uses GPUI Kit 0.7.3 from https://github.com/dux-web/gpui-component at
ee02d7de35215faa68cf31534841c861d02a99cc (Apache-2.0), based on the official
stable sources at https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit, commit
67265a36e260ffe03c5aaebdcd8d654dbf892eab. The fork backports the macOS GPUI Fast
WebView composition adapter from official commit
29c04574dc838a8e59e84c9c9f3c4d15983222ce,
https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/pull/3389, submitted as the stable backport
at https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/pull/3519. The fork also honors explicit
Tab flex-shrink and minimum-size styles on indicator wrappers, from source commit
91dfcff2ddb10c0ca3be45bb4ca8739cc4fc607f, submitted separately at
https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/pull/3522. It also releases tooltip
overlay ownership when a trigger unmounts without hiding a newer trigger's
tooltip, submitted at https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit/pull/3528. It
preserves the stable Kit APIs and editor overlay routing; it does not include
the later inherited-mask clipping change or add Windows composition or Linux
hosting. The Kit packages select GPUI Fast 0.1.8 through Kit's gpui-fast
feature. All nine Fast packages use the compatibility distribution at
https://github.com/dux-web/gpui-fast, commit
a2de5859345c314077b8b81cfe6b34d6d013dcb1. It is generated with the official
release exporter from source commit 90f1ec3153638082560f74a49440cf86bf7a893d,
based on upstream v0.1.8 at d599978f0ecf794b16cb6ec0b5875f818b822507.
The source corrections restore retained child links after reparenting, submitted
at https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-fast/pull/68, and limit the default macOS
overlay's input to interactive GPUI hit regions while preserving native
descendants and custom GPUI surface input, submitted at
https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-fast/pull/69. The distribution retains
Apache-2.0 licenses and upstream attribution, with Sailry modification notices
in the five changed files and distribution NOTICE files.
GPUI WebView owns native composition on macOS with GPUI Fast. Upstream packages retain their license files;
Sailry's current dependency notices and license copies remain in
third_party_licenses/.

